152 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 108 0 R
/E (Quantum Computers can break the current traditional encryption systems - like the RSA \(Rivest-Shamir-Adleman\) and the ECC \(Elliptic Curve Cryptography\). These traditional encryption methods are based on NP-hard problems like integer factorization and discrete logarithms. Classical algorithms to solve these problems scale poorly, requiring exponential time for large inputs. The inability for classical computers to properly solve these problems have made them a great option for data encryption and security. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
